MPU sequence drain can skip object cleanup hooks
Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/81055e54f96081919e5860a059ca711f?repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin&sev=
Criticality: medium
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in commit `4a090db` (`Run object cleanup when MPU order drains pending commands`).

The finding was valid. `reserve_completed_multipart_upload_order` could observe
a pending object metadata command in the same `(pg_id, bucket)` runtime slot
when the bucket PG and object PG were the same. It then drained that command
through `finish_pending_metadata_command_to_acting_set`, which applies/removes
the metadata command but does not run object-command apply/abandon cleanup hooks.

The fix adds an MPU-order-specific pending-command finisher. Bucket commands,
completed-MPU tombstone commands, and `AdvanceCompletedMultipartUploadSequence`
still use the generic bucket metadata finisher. Object metadata commands are
now dispatched through `finish_pending_object_metadata_command_for_bucket`, so
the existing cleanup hooks run when a same-PG pending object command is
converged or abandoned by MPU order allocation.

Regression coverage was added with a same-PG `DeleteObjectVersion` pending
command. The test forces a partial delete apply failure, calls the MPU order
reservation helper, and asserts that the object command converges, payload
reclaim is enqueued, reclaim metadata exists on all acting nodes, and the
completed MPU sequence advances.

The StorageCluster invariant matrix was also updated to list the new
test-only `test_reserve_completed_multipart_upload_order` helper.

Verification before the fix commit:
- `cargo test -p storage completed_multipart_order_drains_same_pg_object_command_with_cleanup_hooks -- --nocapture`
- `cargo nextest run -p storage`
- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`
- `cargo nextest run`
- `git diff --check`

