# Summary
Introduced: the new MPU sequence reservation logic drains non-sequence pending commands with the generic bucket metadata finish path instead of dispatching object metadata commands through their cleanup-aware pending-command path.
The commit adds reserve_completed_multipart_upload_order(), which checks for any pending command keyed by the bucket metadata PG and bucket. It correctly handles AdvanceCompletedMultipartUploadSequence, but for all other pending commands it calls finish_pending_metadata_command_to_acting_set() directly and removes the pending entry. Pending commands are keyed only by (pg_id, bucket), so when an object's metadata PG is the same as the bucket metadata PG, object metadata commands can also appear under this key. Applying those object commands through finish_pending_metadata_command_to_acting_set() bypasses finish_pending_object_metadata_command_for_bucket(), which is the path that calls after_object_metadata_command_applied() and after_object_metadata_command_abandoned(). Those hooks enqueue stale object payload reclaim, delete staged shards, clear stream upload allocators, and run abort cleanup. In normal races the original requester may still run the hook, but orphaned or retried pending object commands after partial failures can be drained by MPU order reservation without cleanup, causing unreclaimed data and potential disk-space denial of service.

